This has been the case for years, so it seems to work without huge losses.
You have to love this country for it!
The butterfly studies the sign at the escalator: "Wear a long dress, please be careful on the escalator".
If there are two separate instructions, he misjudged in the dress code.
But it's more of a conditional construction, and it's certainly already saved lives.
In the upstairs househousing department, the winged man overturns an espresso-prepared cocktail called "Golden Eye," matching the festival award.
This mix, with which a capsule manufacturer presents itself, does not necessarily receive the price for the best drink.
And George Clooney, who's been campaigning for that brand for years, isn't here that night either.
But between local prominence, box-office and kitchen articles, a face that seems familiar to the observer passes: Peter Farrelly, the director of the opening film.
His leading actor should not be far.
And really: Viggo Mortensen, with soon sixty almost acting like a choirboy, walks through the crowd.
He's not chattered about, he wasn't gawped up, one screeches stealthy at most.
Especially for this restrainment, often misunderstood as uptightness, international stars love this film festival.
