Bavaria: Woman missing for 30 years - police dig after corpse parts
More than 30 years after the disappearance of an 18-year-old from Naila (Hof county), the police are searching for the mortal remains of the woman.
Forces dug up a road near Marxgrün on Saturday.
For this purpose, the road surface and several shifts below were removed, as the police and the public prosecutor's office announced together.
According to new findings, the missing person may not have been buried far away from her place of residence at the time.
The woman has been missing since November 4, 1986.
Investigators didn't rule out a crime at the time, either.
Since last year, the criminal police Hof together with the public prosecutor's office is again working intensively on the case.
Together with scientists from the Technical University of Munich and the Bavarian monument protection authority, the investigators encountered an abnormality under the street near Marxgrün by means of a ground radar.
With the help of a dog trained on the smell of human bones, the officers limited the place to a few meters.
The results of the excavations should be announced in the course of the afternoon.
