At the start of the jubilee, those in charge moved under the sounds of the Spielmannszug from Wiesenbronn through the village to the fairground.
In the already proppy marquee, the chairman of the tourism association, Wolfgang Starz, mayor Jürgen Schulz and wine princess Lisa Kursawe greeted the guests. "60 years to do something like this - this is an insane achievement for a small town with 800 inhabitants.
You can be proud of that," Starz thanked all the helpers.
Wine princess Lisa II later toast symbolically with the guests from the stage.
"It's nice that again so many found their way to Us to Abtswind". Later, "Die Troglauer" provided the atmosphere.
