In Bonn: Ambulance car crashes into taxi
An ambulance stands badly damaged next to a road.
In the collision of the emergency vehicle with a taxi, a 27-year-old passer-by has been fatally injured.
If emergency doctors are summoned, they are supposed to help - preferably even save human lives.
Such a rescue ride took a deadly end for a 26-year-old in Bonn.
Bonn - A 26-year-old pedestrian has been fatally injured in the collision of an ambulance with a taxi in Bonn.
The taxi driver, the emergency doctor and their driver were seriously injured, the police said.
The 46-year-old driver of the ambulance car had run over a red traffic light on Saturday afternoon with blue light and Martinshorn.
He then collided on an intersection with the taxi, which was driving at green.
The doctor's car hurled against a traffic light mast and a tree after the collision.
In the process, he captured the passer-by, who still died at the scene of the accident.
Driver of ambulance and taxi driver seriously injured
The 62-year-old taxi driver and the driver of the ambulance were seriously injured in their vehicles and had to be freed by emergency personnel.
The 29-year-old emergency doctor, who was also seriously injured, was able to free herself, but she could no longer help the pedestrian.
Another summoned ambulance tried to do this - but without success.
The three seriously injured were taken to hospitals.
The police, in close coordination with the Bonn prosecutor's office, is investigating who is to blame for the accident.
