For Christian Wulff, the tenure was too short: as federal president, he was not in Tutzing's Evangelical Academy.
But before and after Wulff was a guest there.
Academy director Udo Hahn reckoned when he proudly said: "All federal presidents and chancellors were already with us". However, it was also a topic that celebrities appeared again and again at the academy at Tutzing Castle, but was also an issue in the presentation of the annual programme.
At the end of October, songwriter Konstantin Wecker attends a conference on spiritual experience in a philosophical perspective. On September 29, the writer Frido Mann attends a conference about his grandfather Thomas Mann.
In the meantime, French President Emmanuel Macron has also pledged: He wants to receive the "Tolerance Prize" awarded to him by the academy personally in Tutzing, which in another category also receives television presenter Dunja Hayali (we reported).
The approximately 80 conferences until mid-2019 have it all.
"Pension is not safe!" reads a conference title.
"SOS on Europe's borders" - that's how the academy describes the "risky and deadly route across the Mediterranean."
"And to a conference on Syria: "Barbarism without limit."
Arms deals, destruction, torture, death - the war derides every humane idea."
The spectrum ranges from structural racism in society to the scissors between rich and poor to the radical change of work through digitization.
