Kumm aims: 'And then we fell in love'
It’s no secret that the U.S. president is North Korea’s ruler Kim despite the nuclear crisis.
Now, however, Trump has made a real declaration of love to his colleague.
This also has to do with Kim's "beautiful letters."
At the tender age of 72, the married US president has pleaded guilty to a new blaze.
The Tragic: It's a long-distance relationship.
In public, Donald Trump made an unusual declaration of love to North Korean leader Kim Jong Un on Saturday.
In front of supporters in the U.S. state of West Virginia, Trump found almost tender words for the half-so-old sprout of the ruling dynasty from Pyongyang, even that he turns out to be quite tough chunk in the struggle for North Korea's nuclear disarmament.
"I've been badass, so was he, and between us it went back and forth," Trump reported.
And then we fell in love.
All right?
