Augsburg-based Hannes Aigner has won the gold medal at the end of the Canoe Lalom World Championships in Rio de Janeiro.
The 29-year-old put in a perfect run on Sunday's Olympic track.
Two years ago, he had still missed Olympic bronze by three hundredths of a second.
I was well prepared, had enough rides here at the facility and everything was right today," said the Olympic third from London 2012.
In the finish, he threw away his paddle with joy and stretched both arms confident of victory - knowing that it would be enough for at least one medal.
