He's one of seven Germans in the competition.
In total, 82 candidates from more than 20 countries tried to qualify for the competition.
Grüß was already two years ago as a 14-year-old in Bielefeld.
With terms such as superbrain, genius or prodigy, organizer Laue can do little.
"Head calculation can be trained," he said.
Many participants practiced several hours a day.
In India or Singapore there are even stage-oriented calculation competitions.
Disciplines include, for example, square root drawing from six-figure numbers.
In versatility calculation, the candidates receive surprise tasks, for which they quickly have to find a solution strategy.
Germans would also have good chances here, the chief referee said.
Otherwise Asians are often at an advantage, because head calculations are learned more intensively and with other effective methods already in early childhood.
