Thereafter, the award could take place.
A total of 50 plots for single and semi-detached houses will be created on the site in the south of Landsham, as well as four areas for apartment buildings, each with eight residential units.
The development is now almost complete, the roads and paths are to be paved soon.
An individual property as well as two of the multi-family houses belong to a private person, the rest of the municipality of Pliening.
It sells the majority on the open market, 20 plots of land in a socially acceptable model.
According to Frick, the municipality’s two multi-family homes are to be built as affordable housing.
With a total of 16 income-oriented apartments sponsored by the Free State.
Case for 200 people
Roughly estimated, housing for about 200 people is being created on the area of the Landsham-South development area.
Not only that: Now, at the beginning of October, according to Frick, there will be the start for the new construction of a day-care center.
It is intended to house three kindergarten and three crèche groups as well as a multi-purpose room.
The opening is scheduled for September 2019, at the start of the next kindergarten year.
That's how Schalke's Naldo "great sport" also succeeds on the bench
For the third time in a row not in the starting eleven: Nevertheless, Naldo thanks Schalke coach Domenico Tedesco.
Gelsenkirchen - After Ronaldo Aparecido Rodrigues had not sat in the Schalker starting eleven for the third time in a row, but on the exchange bench, the understanding would have been great for many people, if the almost two-meter-tall Brazilian had really spoken the frustration from the soul.
But when the Schalker players gathered in the middle circle as usual after the 1:0 victory over FSV Mainz 05 and thanked head coach Domenico Tedesco for all his pros, the 36-year-old, whom everyone calls Naldo for the sake of simplicity, intervened and said; "We've got to thank coach!"
"That was very emotional, that was great sport," Tedesco later said of the reaction of his vice-captain, who, despite his reservist existence, harbored no resentment.
Wahrscheinlích knows Naldo, who was hailed as the best Schalker last season, that he actually didn't get on the siding at his coach - but given a break for good reasons.
One reason called "burden control."
It wasn't easy to tell him
"It wasn't easy to tell him, I'll tell you honestly," Tedesco reported from the moment he had told Naldo he wasn't in the starting eleven.
He's an important player, he's an important person.
But it's always about the thing, it's about the club," Tedesco justified the move.
Naldo has played 90 minutes against Bayern and Porto.
He's 36 years old.
It is important that everyone can take a breather at the moment.
And that we're all in the boast," Tedesco explained of the rotation, which Naldo also caught most recently.
And the Brazilian reacted to with the wisdom of his advanced age: by also proving himself an exemplary team player on the bench.
The mood in Austria's industry accelerated its downturn in August compared to the eurozone.
The Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) was on a 37-month low at 46.7 points.
Across Europe, Austria nevertheless has the third-best mood behind Ireland and the Netherlands, the Markit Institute said on Monday on its survey of 3,000 companies.
In contrast than in Austria, the PMI of the euro zone rose by 1.1 to 45.1 points, the index is still below the mark of 50 points for the 13 months in a row, which indicates growth.
Only Ireland's industry cracked that threshold with 50.9 points in August.
The bottom light was the Greeks (42.1 points).
In Germany, France and Spain, the mood barometer declined, but slower than in the months before.
In Spain, the index hit the highest level at 44.0 points since March.
"While the slightly attenuated descent could mean that the worst is over," Markit economist Rob Dobson said.
But in the third quarter, the industry remains the number one growth brake.
A rapid return to the growth zone is not in sight: export orders in the eurozone fell as sharply as not since November 2011.
The companies therefore cut jobs for the seventh month in a row.
In China, too, industrial production fell more sharply in August than initially assumed.
The mood barometer fell to 47.6 points from 49.3 points the previous month.
Experts had initially expected 47.8 points.
The Purchasing Managers Index bases its figures on representative surveys of 3,000 European industrial companies.
Among other things, developments in sales, employment, warehouses and prices are collected.
Tuchel's PSG team achieves eighth victory in the eighth league game
September 29, 2018 at 7:45 P.m
Nice coach Thomas Tuchel rushes from victory to victory with Paris Saint-Germain in France's football championship.
At the OGC Nice, the defending champion won thanks to two goals from superstar Neymar with 3:0 (1:0) and was thus also successful in the eighth league game.
Olympique Lyon last made such a good start to the season in France 82 years ago.
Brazilian Neymar put PSG in the lead after 22 minutes and established the final score in the aftermath.
Christopher Nkunku (46.) provided the interim 2:0.
As a result, Paris also won the dress rehearsal for Wednesday's groundbreaking second Champions League group game against Red Star Belgrade.
At the kick-off of the premier class, Tuchel's team at 2:3 in Liverpool had to accept the only mandatory game defeat so far this season.
